Turn a useful-material definition into an explicit supply agreement (@cs-agreement: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @chemical-supply-systems, #source "../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY", #source "../sources/Validation-Including-Sampling-Eurachem.lingua#r_0H2SA2SC85XXDYT629N3E3KGXA", #source "../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME", #chemical-supply-systems "../foundations/Draw-material-information-money-and-responsibility-separately.lingua#r_12722F6QK2K31GCEZEJYMYSP5H") { r_3J12DD0DDF2HT8EJXNRC7NSE3E
**Read:** [Good trade and distribution practices for pharmaceutical starting materials — WHO](../sources/Pharmaceutical-Starting-Materials-WHO.lingua#r_7H51215T44S69TD3R0499VMTTY), the complete quality, procurement, documentation and contract sections; [Validation of Measurement Procedures that Include Sampling — Eurachem](../sources/Validation-Including-Sampling-Eurachem.lingua#r_0H2SA2SC85XXDYT629N3E3KGXA), the entire purpose, target-uncertainty and integrated-measurement discussion; [Caustic Soda Handbook — OxyChem](../sources/Caustic-Soda-Handbook-OxyChem.lingua#r_1MRFTA19NDBFBQXC69CCRQPAME), actual producer grade/specification and analytical-method material.

After the shared product-specification Record, describe the actual agreement between a supplier and a receiving user. State the product, quantity basis, impurity panel, physical state, analytical methods, representative sample, reporting uncertainty where relevant, acceptance decision and response to a nonconforming delivery. The specification needs to identify whose operation will be affected and which evidence will be available when.

Use one hypothetical impurity with a maximum limit. Compare a producer's batch average, a terminal tank sample and a package sample at receipt: these can represent different targets even when the method is identical. Specify how a changed feed source, process, packaging material or distribution route will be communicated and evaluated. A sales label such as technical, analytical or electronic does not replace this content.

Write two plausible agreements for the same nominal chemical and explain their tradeoffs. One may require an additional contaminant measurement and a release delay; another may permit a qualified producer's report under continuing evidence of performance. Neither should promise impossible certainty. Distinguish technical acceptance from title, payment and liability provisions, and use appropriate commercial/legal sources when those provisions become part of the actual case.

